# AGENT.md — src/shared/auth/

JWT authentication. Self-contained: login endpoint, strategy, guard,
decorator, and a request logging interceptor.

## What lives here

- `jwt.strategy.ts` — validates the bearer token, attaches the payload to
  `request.user`.
- `guards/jwt-auth.guard.ts` — apply with `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)` on any
  controller or route that should require a valid token.
- `decorators/current-user.decorator.ts` — `@CurrentUser()` reads
  `request.user` inside a guarded route. Never re-decode the token by hand.
- `interceptors/logging.interceptor.ts` — registered globally in
  `app.module.ts` via `APP_INTERCEPTOR`. Logs every request; not auth-specific,
  it just lives here because it was added alongside auth.
- `auth.service.ts` — **starter-only**. It checks credentials against
  `ADMIN_USER`/`ADMIN_PASSWORD` env vars. Replace `validateUser` with a real
  user lookup and hashed passwords before this is exposed anywhere real.

## Rules

- Feature modules stay public unless you explicitly add
  `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)` to them — this module does not protect anything
  on its own.
- Do not put business-domain logic here. This directory is about proving
  identity, not about what an authenticated user is allowed to do.
